There are additional Winsock2-specific functions that are not supported by the POSIX version of
the Berkeley Socket library, just like most POSIX-compatible operating systems have their own
platform-specific networking functions in addition to the POSIX standard ones. The standard
socket functions provide adequate functionality for a typical multiplayer networked game,
so for the rest of this chapter, we will explore only the standard, cross-platform functions. The
sample code for this book targets the Windows Operating System but uses Winsock2-specific
